  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Table 6-3: BLTC0N1 Code Bits for Octant Line Drawing\n",
      "bbox": [
        172.19000244140625,
        68.22502899169922,
        427.62353515625,
        78.72502899169922
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2865868840498663,
        0.08838812841389408,
        0.7117213238237834,
        0.10199127907666337
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "BLTCON1 Code Bits \nOctant #\n4 3 2\n",
      "bbox": [
        202.44000244140625,
        100.76973724365234,
        395.5559387207031,
        123.97502899169922
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.33693390257353745,
        0.13055103980695976,
        0.6583491627741938,
        0.16061438074240725
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "1 1 0 \n0\n0 0 1 \n1\nO i l \n2\n1 1 1 \n3\n1 0 1 \n4\n0 1 0 \n5\n0 0 0 \n6\n1 0 0 \n7\n",
      "bbox": [
        238.69000244140625,
        139.1240234375,
        381.8365173339844,
        239.60906982421875
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.397267106589507,
        0.18024048110771043,
        0.6355150483050638,
        0.3104226930461768
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 3,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "We initialize BLTCON1 bits 4 through 2 according to the above Table. Now, we introduce the \nvariables dx and dy, and set them to the absolute values of the difference between the x coordi­\nnates and the y coordinates of the endpoints of the line, respectively.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.53500366210938,
        260.80908203125,
        517.7476196289062,
        297.1060791015625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14236140210904125,
        0.337888117818062,
        0.8617206279683693,
        0.38491226255649597
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 4,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "dx = abs(x2 - xl) ; \ndy = abs(y2 - yl) ;\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.88579559326172,
        310.655029296875,
        190.38580322265625,
        329.4689025878906
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1429452476579894,
        0.40246544454022865,
        0.31687132434694476,
        0.42683953529527024
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 5,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Now, we rearrange them if necessary so dx is greater than dy.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.53580474853516,
        345.30035400390625,
        352.9172668457031,
        355.8031005859375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14236273540864847,
        0.4473497847069248,
        0.5873828816926941,
        0.46095649367152064
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 6,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "if (dx < dy)\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.13478088378906,
        369.7169189453125,
        147.90428161621094,
        378.2169189453125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14335964987399938,
        0.47898237628456675,
        0.2461665985541039,
        0.4899944506306181
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 7,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "{\ntemp = dx ; \ndx = dy ; \ndy = temp ;\n",
      "bbox": [
        128.28488159179688,
        378.9001159667969,
        190.3848876953125,
        417.5648498535156
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.21351277057220344,
        0.4908795584416283,
        0.3168698005759651,
        0.540971196574668
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 8,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "}\n",
      "bbox": [
        129.83657836914062,
        418.9500427246094,
        134.87657165527344,
        429.4500427246094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2160953592132628,
        0.5427657667958568,
        0.22448374385247297,
        0.556368917458626
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Alternately, set dx and dy as follows:\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.78857421875,
        443.6972961425781,
        246.23760986328125,
        454.2000427246094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14278343587804102,
        0.574826777913415,
        0.4098290745458223,
        0.5884334868780108
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "dx = max(abs(x2 - xl), abs(y2 - yl)) ; \ndy = min(abs(x2 - xl), abs(y2 - yl)) ;\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.03057861328125,
        467.7489929199219,
        292.54058837890625,
        486.3135681152344
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1431862193403311,
        0.6059866688617436,
        0.4868940965963121,
        0.6300377844209955
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 11,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "These calculations have the effect of “ normalizing” our line into octant 0; since we have already \ninformed the blitter of the real octant to use, it has no difficulty drawing the line.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.53057861328125,
        501.9977722167969,
        517.720947265625,
        525.3457641601562
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1423540372159729,
        0.6503572693180601,
        0.8616762354404953,
        0.6806054838017402
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 12,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "We initialize the A pointer register to 4 * dy - 2 * dx. If this value is negative, we set the sign bit \n(SIGNFLAG in BLTCON1), otherwise we clear it. We set the A modulo register to 4 * (dy - dx) \nand the B modulo register to 4 * dy.\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.03057861328125,
        541.093017578125,
        517.4810180664062,
        577.394775390625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.1431862193403311,
        0.7010066514940677,
        0.8612769058590924,
        0.7480369639556677
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 13,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The A data register should be preloaded with $8000. Both word masks should be set to SFFFF. \nThe A shift value should be set to the x coordinate of the first point (xl) modulo 15.\n",
      "bbox": [
        85.78753662109375,
        592.6937866210938,
        516.8441162109375,
        616.3927612304688
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14278170893759742,
        0.7678574167899025,
        0.8602168691809091,
        0.7985603427103285
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 14,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The B data register should be initialized with the line texture pattern, if any, or $FFFF for a solid \nline. The B shift value should be set to the bit number at which to start the line texture (zero \nmeans the last significant bit.)\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.02651977539062,
        631.341796875,
        517.9967041015625,
        667.8858032226562
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14317946395565462,
        0.8179273888184873,
        0.8621351952595688,
        0.8652715435011887
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 15,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Blitter Hardware 185\n",
      "bbox": [
        420.6000061035156,
        715.3650512695312,
        515.6669921875,
        725.8650512695312
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.7000316131685913,
        0.9267827210761064,
        0.8582577060399945,
        0.9403858717388757
      ]
    }
  ],
